  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1136 PM CDT SAT OCT 24 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will continue to remain the dominant feature\nfor much of the upcoming workweek, with afternoon high\ntemperatures remaining steady in the 70s. Rain chances also\nremain limited over the next seven days, as dry air keeps\npermeating the air column overhead. As we begin to approach the\nweekend, the upper-level ridge will begin to break down, as a\ndeep trough develops to the west. This will put the region into\nSW flow, allowing for our temperatures to slightly climb into the\nweekend, with afternoon highs climbing into the upper-70s and low-\n80s.\n\n/44/",
